+# PKG-02 candidate semantics — Phase A V1
+Status: candidate derivative design, not lifecycle acceptance. Parent HELP_HUMAN; manager WORKING_ITEMS; RunID HELP-HUMAN-PIPING-20260905-UI-TOOLKIT-PARITY. Agent model attribution unknown; native role enforcement instruction-asserted.
+
+## Basis and activation
+PKG-02 only, DEL-02-01 (SOW-041/SOW-065, OUT-001), DEL-02-02 (SOW-025, OUT-001), DEL-02-03 (SOW-002, interface assessment only). ScopeOfWork.md files are SOW_V1. Current decomposition revision 0.12, SCA-009 accepted Vocabulary Annex rows 19–21/24, approved DAG-010 via execution/_DAG/_LATEST.md. Relevant invariants docs/CONTRACT.md OPS-K-ID-1, OPS-K-DATA-2/3, OPS-K-UNIT-1. DEL-02-02 U-003/U-006/U-008/U-013 apply. DEL-02-01 and DEL-02-03 Remaining empty; this is not evidence of completion. DEL-02-02 open alias/parser/diagnostic-policy and independent numeric-validation residuals remain open.
+
+Scope: define implementable payload/reference rules; PKG-16 owns executable resolvers and PKG-07 consumes UI contracts. No code, schemas, lifecycle, DAG, annex, or governing truth mutation. Outputs are run-local derivative evidence. Single integration owner N3. Graph V1: manager draft + independent reviewer (read-only source, own evidence file only), then serial manager fan-in. No sibling coordination.
+
+## Row 19 split/insert node in straight pipe
+Candidate change kind split_pipe_run. Explicit payload pipe_ref, fraction strictly between 0 and 1, new_node {id,label,provenance}, new_pipe {id,label,provenance}; source snapshot/hash through existing operation envelope. Fraction is dimensionless, all values finite. Position interpolates from to to using the model project coordinate unit. Existing source ID remains first segment from original from to new node; new pipe runs new node to original to. Original endpoints unchanged. Preserve every source pipe physical field (section/material/y_reference and supported metadata); source label/provenance unchanged; new records use explicit labels/provenance. Global ID collisions fail, including duplicate payload IDs.
+Reject zero-length source, unsupported/non-straight component geometry, every component geometry reference to the source pipe, element-targeted primitive loads, wind exposed_pipe_refs/exposed_spans, and any unsupported reference requiring repartition. Do not silently choose one half for a load or component. Endpoint nodal supports/loads remain unchanged and retain their original node intent. Result invalidation follows existing operation pipeline. This first executable slice is node insertion/straight split; finite-length component insertion is not claimed complete.
+
+## Row 20 geometry copy/rotate/mirror
+Candidate change kind transform_pipe_run; explicit mode copy or in_place, explicit pipe_refs, explicit transform kind translate/rotate/mirror. Translation has quantity-valued x/y/z; rotation has quantity-valued origin, nonzero finite axis vector and explicit angle+unit; mirror has quantity-valued plane origin and nonzero finite normal. No default axis/origin/angle. Rotation/mirror use model coordinates after conversion through accepted unit functions. Reflection is about supplied plane, not merely sign flip about origin.
+Copy requires exact explicit ID map and labels/provenance for every selected pipe and unique endpoint node; no ID reuse, auto-numbering or hidden joining. References between copied nodes/pipes remap; material and section data retain meaning; originals unchanged. In_place retains IDs and requires selected nodes not incident to any unselected pipe to prevent hidden geometry mutation. All modes reject supports, node/pipe primitive loads, components, wind exposure references or unsupported attached engineering data touching affected nodes/pipes: this is a bounded geometry-only slice, with blockers enumerating affected IDs. Do not quietly omit attachments. Copy rejection avoids implying a complete supported/loaded run was cloned.
+Transform y_reference as direction (no translation); reject degenerate resulting frame. No new stiffness/load assumptions. Reflection support/load transformations, especially moment pseudovectors and restraint-axis behavior, are outside this first bounded slice. Reject source objects with unknown geometry-dependent extension fields instead of retaining uninterpreted orientation data. Preserve pipe scalar properties. Full connected physical-run copy including attached supports/components/loads remains residual.
+
+## Row 24 display contract
+Session-only DisplayUnitSystem = entered | si | us_customary, default entered. No model operation, dirty flag, model hash change, undo checkpoint, project.units mutation, export payload rewrite, or solver input change. Central pure display function consumes source value+unit+dimension and optional preferred target; returns displayed value/unit plus exact entered source and diagnostic on unavailable conversion. UI keeps entered-authoring fields authoritative; toggling never writes rounded converted values into drafts. Unsupported dimensions/units retain entered display with explicit unconverted indicator. Affine temperature and temperature-difference semantics must stay distinct; never route temperature through multiplicative-only table. Reuse accepted DEC-018 core/units catalog/conversion authority; do not parse prose factor_representation. Existing frontend unitConversion.ts is a limited display table, not comprehensive unit authority. Implement available catalog dimensions, and explicitly disclose dimensions not converted rather than inventing aliases/constants. Cross-surface acceptance: viewport coordinate readouts, inspector and grid quantity readouts use one context; editable fields retain entered units; model serialized bytes/hash invariant across toggles.
+
+## Row 21 ownership assessment
+SCA-009 assigns DEL-02-03 + DEL-04-03. DEL-02-03 actual SOW is mechanics/user-rule/professional-acceptance state separation, not a nozzle mechanics law. Nozzle/equipment semantic labeling cannot imply nozzle allowable checks, equipment flexibility, or validation. PKG-04 must confirm whether existing explicit DOF/stiffness support mechanics represent the intended bounded boundary; PKG-02 can preserve code-neutral status and references only. Do not infer an anchor is the user's nozzle boundary. Hold new nozzle mechanics; existing explicit supports remain available.
+
+## Alternatives and acceptance evidence
+Split retains source as first child instead of replacing both IDs: minimizes unrelated identity churn, but blocks references whose meaning would change. Geometry-only transform avoids inventing vector/restraint mechanics; later full physical-run transform requires typed attachment rules. Session display preference avoids changing entered-units-preserved persistence. Required implementation tests: split topology/length conservation and stable original endpoint attachments; collision/fraction/degenerate/reference rejection; rotation/mirror/translation explicit numeric fixtures, y_reference behavior, copy originals unchanged and in-place boundary rejection; atomic failure and stale hash; native/Wasm preview/apply parity; display invariant hash, units/dimensions and no draft mutation. Findings/design acceptance by parent is required before dependent code.
+
+## V2 independent-refutation disposition (supersedes conflicting V1 wording)
+R1 accepted: validate finite stored new coordinates and both realized segment lengths against existing consuming-engine nondegeneracy policy after interpolation, including endpoint rounding/overflow fixtures. R2 accepted: these resolvers apply ONLY openpipestress.product_preview.model in supported schema version, not canonical model.schema.yaml Element. Guard matrix: component.node; component.geometry bend_pipe_ref/branch_header_pipe_ref/branch_branch_pipe_ref/rigid_pipe_ref/expansion_joint_pipe_ref; supports.node; primitive_loads target.node/pipe/support; equivalent_static_generation.wind exposed_pipe_refs and exposed_spans[].pipe_ref; incident unselected pipes for in-place; unknown reference-bearing extensions and unknown geometric fields on selected node/pipe records. Split permits unchanged endpoint supports/nodal loads but blocks pipe-based component/loads/wind references. Translate preserves absent y_reference; rotate/mirror requires explicit nondegenerate y_reference rather than synthesizing orientation. R3 accepted in ROW17_CANDIDATE_V2. All findings are implementation constraints, not new human gates. Row21 needs PKG04 ownership assessment rather than blanket human decision; existing DOF mechanics may support explicit boundary labeling.
